    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d306">

                <pb facs="0596" n="526" xml:id="pg526"/>

                <head>No. 306.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. West.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-07-30"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 30,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Acknowledging the receipt of your note of
                    the 25th instant concerning the alleged stealing of horses from Canadian
                    territory by South Piegan Indians from the United States, I have the honor to
                    inform you that the proper authorities of this Government have been requested to
                    investigate the matter, with a view to having such action taken as may be found
                    to be proper.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
